 ## Background
-The method originates from early volume rendering techniques that combined ray tracing with volume data [S1, unofficial]. The integration of classical ray tracing into volume rendering pipelines was proposed to handle visibility and geometric merging, such as superimposing radiation treatment planning isodose surfaces over CT data [S4, unofficial]. The heuristic shading approach was developed to balance performance and visual quality in scientific visualization [S2, unofficial]. Recent applications include integrating ray tracing for interreflections in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S5, unofficial].
